  "recent_notes": [
    "The Vice President, Finance and Planning post at New Brunswick Community College is the evening's most substantial signal, and it sits comfortably within the region you are moving toward, a short drive from where family waits. Public sector finance rewards precisely what your record contains: budget discipline, capital planning, and the patience to steward an institution rather than merely report on it. The search will still take the time it takes. Long voyages are won by steady watches, not by favourable weather. I would suggest you draft the NBCC application this week and include one paragraph naming how you would modernize its finance operations, AI included, within an existing budget. Make it so.",
    "A finance leader who can direct these tools, rather than merely tolerate them, has become a scarce commodity, and scarcity is leverage. Tonight's reading is brief but pointed: directing an AI system asks much the same discipline as directing a capable analyst, which you have practiced across decades of closes. Note also the Head of Finance and Operations post at Inspekt AI. A company built on this technology will question you about it, and your answer should be operational rather than fashionable: where it removes days from a close, and where it must never come near a control. Might I recommend you write half a page this week on how you would deploy AI within a finance function you have actually run. Make it so.",
    "Consider the fractional route not as a lesser berth but as a side door held open. Firms that cannot yet fund a permanent seat will still pay handsomely for judgment, and judgment is precisely what decades of closes, capital plans, and hard operating winters produced. An interim engagement in the Halifax area would put you inside the regional network within weeks rather than months, and in a smaller market that network is how the permanent seats are quietly filled. The construction post on Boston's South Shore deserves an application as well. Keep both lines in the water. Might I recommend you write to two Halifax advisory or private equity contacts this week, offering interim finance capacity in plain terms. Make it so.",
    "Three seats surfaced tonight within reach of home, and two of them come through the same house. That is worth noticing. In a market the size of Nova Scotia's, a small number of search firms hold the door to nearly every serious finance mandate, and they place people they have met before they place resumes that arrive unannounced. Your record of closes, capital plans and plant floor decisions reads well on paper. It reads considerably better in twenty minutes of conversation with a partner who can then vouch for you. The Commissionaires post in Bedford deserves a formal application. The relationship deserves rather more than that. Might I recommend you request a standing introductory call with a Venor partner this week, independent of any single posting."
  ],
